senses.gloss:
द्वन्द्वम् + .{@-न्द्वः@}
—1 (In gram.) One of the four principal kinds of compounds, in which two
 or more words are joined together which, if not compounded, would stand
 in the same case and be connected by the copulative conjunction ‘and’;
 चार्थे द्वन्द्वः P. II. 2. 29; द्वन्द्वः सामासिकस्य च Bg. 10. 33;
 उभयपदप्रधानो द्वन्द्वः Kāśi. 38.
—2 A kind of disease. —3 (in music) A kind of measure.
—4 The sign Gemini of the zodiac.
